All five are listed consequences of global warming and the rising CO2 behind it:

- the hydrological cycle intensifies (more evaporation, heavier rain and droughts);
- species migrate towards the poles and to higher altitudes;
- warming and melting ice change ocean circulation;
- the oceans absorb more CO2 and become more acidic;
- sea level rises from thermal expansion and melting ice.

So the answer is option (D).
